b_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4, 4.5, 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you press the \"Focus\" key (default is `F`) while any subgizmo of any gizmo is selected, the viewport camera will frame itself around a completely non-sensical point in space instead of the selection. It's easiest to check using `Path3D` node, but it happens with everything, including custom gizmos.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd843178-e5c6-4e59-b373-641f46ebc863\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open attached scene\n- Select the path\n- Select one of its vertices using the `Select Points` tool\n- Press the focus key\n- Observe that the camera focuses on the wrong place\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25681786/bug-report.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":